      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name came from a property purchased by Barnes, who called it Hollywood Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://hpcatx.com/history-hp/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mecca Drive, now Highway 16, originally linked Hollywood Park to San Pedro, showing early road planning.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://hpcatx.com/history-hp/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1975, the town’s Administration and Police Departments moved into a former lumber yard at 2 Mecca Drive, repurposing historic buildings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://hollywoodpark-tx.gov/about/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hollywood Park sits about 15 miles north of downtown San Antonio, nestled in the Texas Hill Country.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
